# Demo decoys - simple small molecules / fragments, presumed non-binders.
# Format: <SMILES> <name>
# NOTE ON RIGOR: these bundled decoys are deliberately simple for a runnable demo.
# A real validation uses PROPERTY-MATCHED decoys (e.g. DUD-E / DEKOIS) so that
# enrichment reflects binding, not a trivial molecular-weight or logP artifact.
# The validation harness (src/validate.py) is decoy-agnostic; swap this file for a
# property-matched decoy set for a defensible benchmark.
c1ccccc1 benzene
Oc1ccccc1 phenol
Cc1ccccc1 toluene
Nc1ccccc1 aniline
Clc1ccccc1 chlorobenzene
c1ccncc1 pyridine
c1ccc2ccccc2c1 naphthalene
CCO ethanol
CO methanol
CCCO propanol
CCCCCC hexane
C1CCCCC1 cyclohexane
CC(=O)C acetone
CC(=O)O acetic_acid
CCCC(=O)O butanoic_acid
OCC(O)CO glycerol
NC(=O)N urea
CCN ethylamine
COC dimethyl_ether
CCCCCCCCCCCC dodecane
